{"id":"int-7826fff830ee0e79f2312924c64025a4","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-18T13:56:24.247579202Z","actor":"Anthony Green","issue_id":"scute-7wi","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Moved to keyfence's own tracker as keyfence-lls, now that keyfence has one. The fix is entirely in keyfence's code."}}
{"id":"int-93b5629f8341ddd63169889f58eb21da","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-18T13:56:24.99332932Z","actor":"Anthony Green","issue_id":"scute-35m","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Moved to keyfence's tracker as keyfence-0rk. Needs broker-side SO_PEERCRED support; scute's half is just passing the cgroup."}}
{"id":"int-13602d52cb7e2364008c69566cfdaec4","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-18T14:16:28.424279843Z","actor":"Anthony Green","issue_id":"scute-vqg","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed in keyfence cdc80e0. Over the 10 MiB inspection limit the prefix is spliced back in front of the rest of the stream and the whole response goes to the client with Content-Length untouched; rules are skipped rather than run on a fragment, and the audit trail records that with rule_action 'skipped' and a reason. A response with no rules to run is no longer buffered at all.\n\nCovered by the repository's first Go tests (5, in internal/proxy/response_test.go), which were checked against the previous code to confirm they fail on it -- declared-length and chunked oversized cases, inspection still happening under the limit, rule state still accumulating, and no buffering when there is nothing to inspect. CI runs go test ./... now."}}
{"id":"int-063cd8b68d3baa275183a91a81232f7e","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-18T14:32:00.27869719Z","actor":"Anthony Green","issue_id":"scute-but","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed in keyfence: an empty destination list now permits nothing, issuance refuses an omitted or empty list with a 400 naming ['*'] as the explicit alternative, and the SSH bastion refuses a wildcard. Scute was already safe here -- it requires a non-empty list and rejects '*' -- so nothing changes on this side."}}
{"id":"int-12a00c215954cdf07f79cba41faeb248","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-18T14:36:48.806889392Z","actor":"Anthony Green","issue_id":"scute-rdt","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed in keyfence: the bastion now authenticates upstream hosts against a known_hosts file instead of ssh.InsecureIgnoreHostKey, refusing unknown hosts and mismatched keys with distinct audit reasons. -ssh-insecure-host-keys is the explicit waiver."}}
{"id":"int-0693a2cac93e3bb383463a31953c6968","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-18T14:50:04.920949857Z","actor":"Anthony Green","issue_id":"scute-8fe","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed in keyfence 101cfb6 both ways: a reaper forgets credential material once no valid token references it (at once on revoke, within a minute for expiry), and credentials can now be registered by name so scute-minted tokens need not copy a secret in at all."}}
